<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62610" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευγᾰλέος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λυγρός</span>): <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> of persons,
				<i>in sad</i> or <i>sorry plight, wretched</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτωχῷ λ. ἐναλίγκιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.273
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἐσόμεσθα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.61
				</span></i>
			. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, χωρεῖν</span> to go <i>in ill plight</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				13.723
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of
			conditions, etc., <i>sore, baneful</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῦν
				δέ με λ. θανάτῳ εἵμαρτο ἁλῶναι</span>, i.e. by
			drowning, <i><span class="en">
				21.281
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.359
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κήδεσιν . . λευγαλέοισι</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				399
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλγεσι λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					20.203
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολέμοιο μεθήσετε λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.97
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δαῒ λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.387
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρεσὶ λ. πιθήσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.119
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἐπέεσσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					20.109
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤθεα λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					525
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποινή</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				754
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					1174
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνῖαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.295
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέντρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					836
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> rarely of
			material objects, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. χιτών</span>
			<i>sorry</i> tunic, <i><span class="en">
				Philet.
				17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευγαλέα: διάβροχος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				561.28
			</span></i> (prob. an error due to misunderstanding of <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				785
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
